  "comment": "Sumber: https://www.arduino.cc/en/Tutorial/SerialEvent This example demonstrates use of the SerialEvent() function. This function is called inside the loop(). If there is serial data in the buffer each character found is added to a string until a newline is found. In this case the string made by the characters received so far is printed and set back to null. Hardware Arduino or Genuino Board Code",
